API-24: switch the numeric locale per thread, never for the process

PR #919 made EN_createproject and the legacy createtmpfiles call
setlocale(LC_NUMERIC, "") so that the report uses the system's decimal
separator, and made saveinpfile switch to "C" and back to "". setlocale
is process-wide, so the host program's own numbers changed too. New
helpers in project.c, setnumericlocale() and restorenumericlocale(),
change the calling thread's locale only (uselocale on POSIX,
_configthreadlocale on Windows). They wrap saveinpfile ("C") and the
report output ("") in EN_open, EN_runH, EN_nextH, EN_report and
writemassbalance(). The Windows code has not been compiled or run.

FILE-02 changes the first lines of saveinpfile() too, so this patch
is made on top of it.

Requires: FILE-02

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb, after FILE-02:
    git apply FILE-02_fix.patch
    git apply API-24_fix.patch

